## DESCRIPTION
## Calculus Two, Sequences
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Infinite sequences and series)
## DBsection(Limit of a sequence)
## Date(09/16/2018)
## Institution(Community College of Denver, Colorado Community College System)
## Author(Brittni Lorton)
## KEYWORDS('calculus', 'sequences', 'formula of a sequence','find explicit formula from recursive')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "PGcourse.pl");

Context('Numeric')->variables->are(n => "Real");

$a                = random(2, 5);
$f                = Formula("$a^n");
$f->{test_points} = [ [1], [2], [3], [4], [5], [6] ];

BEGIN_PGML

Find a function, [`f(n)`], that identifies the [`n`]th term of the following recursively defined sequence as [`a_n=f(n)`].

[```a_1=[$a] \quad\text{and} \quad a_{n+1}=[$a]a_n \quad \text{for}\quad n \geq 1.```]

[`f(n)=`][_]{$f}{10}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
This is a geometric sequence with [`r=[$a]`] so the formula is 
[``` f(n) = [$f]```] 
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
